I crouch low to the ground, trying not to make any noise as I creep towards the source of the sounds. My heart thumps in my chest, but I force myself to stay calm - we can't afford to draw attention to ourselves here, especially from hostile humans. 

Suddenly, a faint light flickers through the trees ahead. Cautiously, I move closer until I catch sight of two figures hunched around a campfire. One is clad in tattered leather armor, carrying an axe on his shoulder; the other wears worn-out traveler's clothes and holds a torch.

They're talking about us - or rather, our belongings: "That fancy gear they got must be worth a fortune," whispers the man in leather armor. His companion nods in agreement. 

"We should take what we can and leave them for the monsters," he says with a sinister grin.

